James wrote:
> Doug Freyburger <dfrey...@yahoo.com> wrote:
>> Purgatorios wrote:
>
>> > Should I spend my scrolls of enchant weapon/armor, magic
>> > marker etc.  or wait until I get better stuff?
>
>> The enchant weapon definitely.  Dip for water so you have lots
>> of holy water then read them blessed.  The more enchanted the
>> better the searching function for Excalibur.
>
> Up to a point.  Use id to find out how far they're already
> enchanted, and don't use enchant weapon if they're more than +5.

If I read the code correctly an "s" starts out with a 1-in-7 chance of
succeeding.  If you are wielding Excalibur is enchantment gets added up
to a 6-in-7 chance maximum.  After +5 further enchantment of Excalibur
no longer matters for searching but it still matters for damage.  Insert
here the usual caveat about over-enhanted weapons evaporating.

Thinking about this I would not want to wander the dungeon wielding the
cursed -2 rustproot Excalibur when I want to search for something.

>> > chaotic altar on lvl 11
>
>> I like to keep one cross aligned altar just in case.  I convert the
>> rest.
>
> You need at least one co-aligned one.  If the chaotic is the
> only altar, then convert it.

It can't be the only altar because of the one in the mines.  If the one
in the mines was co-aligned or you killed the priest to convert it then
this one should be kept cross-aligned.  If the one in the mines was
cross-aligned and you left the priest alive I would definitely convert
it.  Having at least one co-aligned altar is so important I have killed
the mine town priest for one.  Having one cross-aligned altar is a nice
to have just in case.

>> Probably not worth enhancing spells until you have XP slots to
>> spare.  You will get a huge gain from bow to expert and
>> a smaller but large gain from moving twoweapon up.
>
> I'd increase bow to expert, and twoweapon to skilled, before I'd
> start thinking about spells.

Skill slot strategy should be thought out in advance.  It can be
tempting to enhance a skill slot just because you get the offer.  Resist
that temptation unless the offer matches your long term plan or it is
for your immediate survival.

>> Permantent light.
>
> Or a likely wish.  (But as you say, since the castle wand is so
> close, it's probably not worth it now.)

And it's already been posted elsewhere in the thread that a guaranteed
permanent light source does not equal a guaranteed wish.


